            '{"parser": "legacy-migration", "file_name": "jeen buddy guidelines - Nir.docx", "file_type": "docx", "legacyData": {"legacy_id": "441629f9-c5f6-44c0-9fde-b91de0034a8b", "external_id": null, "collection": "collection", "type": "chunk-data", "tags": "", "user_id": "857ca8ca4fc24d6afbf9ff5b74818b87", "create_date": "2026-04-12T08:15:52.512Z", "link_to_file": "https://jeenfilesdevweu.blob.core.windows.net/jeendocs/857ca8ca4fc24d6afbf9ff5b74818b87/data/1775981749419-jeen buddy guidelines - Nir.docx", "excerptKeywords": "KEYWORDS: הצטרפות, עובד חדש, Buddy, שבוע ראשון, שאלות"}}'::jsonb,
            '2026-04-12T08:15:52.512000+00:00',
            $TRANS$Things to do the day before joining contact with the new employee (preferably in the morning). Introduce yourself as his Buddy. Make sure he knows how to get to the office on the first day. Check if he has any questions before starting work. The first week of the first week is recommended to be a little more present and check in with the new employee on a daily basis how things are progressing. Say hello and introduce yourself on the first day. Schedule a short introductory conversation. Help the new employee understand a little about the team and people. Initiate shared lunches and coffee breaks. Be available for small questions that arise during the day.$TRANS$
        );
